    "summary": "High‑energy NYE with soaring Lovelight & explosive Tower of Power jam",
    "blurb": "The Oakland Auditorium show bursts with high energy, highlighted by the third‑set Turn On Your Lovelight featuring guest vocalist Etta James and a fiery Tower of Power horn section. Jerry’s guitar shines throughout, especially during the Space → NFA improvisation, while the rhythm section drives the first two sets with tight precision.",
    "review": "The Dead lit up Oakland Auditorium on New Year's Eve ’82 with a relentless drive that only a holiday crowd can fuel. The first two sets rolled tight, from the crisp opener “Cold Rain And Snow” through a seamless Sugar Magnolia → Sugaree segue into a scorching Playing In The Band > Drums > Space > Not Fade Away sequence. The highlight arrives in the third set when Etta James joins for “Turn On Your Lovelight”, and the band locks with Tower of Power’s brass for an explosive horn jam that carries through “Tell Mama” and “Hard To Handle”. Jerry Garcia is on fire, his lead cutting through even the dense mix, while the Space → NFA stretch showcases a fluid, exploratory dialogue between guitar and keyboards. Brent’s keys fill out the texture, and Mickey and Billy drive each groove with tight, propulsive drumming that never loses its swing.",
